      "evidence_excerpts": [
        "As we have seen, the sense of personal identity given by episodic memory is robust — it gives us an ‘irresistible’ sense of being the same person, and it has seemed to many to be a necessary concomitant of episodic memory. But the case of R.B. indicates that this sense of identity is dissociable from episodic memory itself. The sense of identity turns out to be, pace Reid, a contingent feature of memory."
