        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Limits And Interpretation",
        "body": "The argument is cautious about what follows for metaphysics. R.B. does not settle whether personal identity is psychological, biological, or something else, and the neural details of the ownership mechanism remain incomplete. The practical lesson is narrower but important: before treating memory as evidence for identity, philosophers should ask how the ownership-producing system works and how reliable it is.",
