 Necessity, and Explanation\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The grounding and essence sources provide a contrast class for this contingency claim. Trogdon's account treats full grounding as metaphysically necessitating what is grounded through essence, while Correia and Skiles argue that generalized identity can distinguish genuine essence from merely necessary entailment or coextension.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Synthesis Constraint\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The synthesis should be careful: the memory source does not present a formal grounding theory, and the grounding sources do not analyze episodic memory. The shared topic is that identity-involving appearances may need decomposition before they can support claims of essence-like necessity.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\\\",\n        \\\"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Contingent Selfhood and Essential Explanation\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-contingent-selfhood-and-essential-explanation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-the-evidential-force-of-memory-for-personal-identity-depends-on-the-contingent-c--ef23d993b2fe\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-memory-based-sense-of-personal-identity-depends-on-at-least-two-separable-co--f9eaee4ce165\\\",\n        \\\"claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-perceived-emotional-synchrony-during-the-psychedelic-ceremony-mediates-later-cha--adcb9ca374b4\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\\\",\n        \\\"claim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Psychological Conditions on Metaphysical Commitment\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The memory and psychedelic-belief sources jointly support a topic on how metaphysical commitments may be shaped by contingent psychological systems rather than by argument alone. In the memory case, ownership feelings affect the evidential force of memory for personal identity; in the psychedelic studies, ceremonies and psilocybin therapy are associated with shifts away from hard materialism.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Mediating Mechanisms\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The shared concept is mediation. R.B.'s dissociation suggests that the sense of diachronic identity depends on mechanisms supplying mineness, while the psychedelic source reports emotional synchrony and baseline peer conformity as predictors or mediators of later non-physicalist belief change.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Epistemic Rather Than Refutational Force\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The topic should not claim that these mechanisms refute the metaphysical views involved. The stronger supported point is epistemic: local evidence suggests that some intuitions or commitments about selfhood, physicalism, and identity are sensitive to cognitive and social conditions.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\\\",\n        \\\"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Cognitive Mediators of Metaphysical Commitment\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-cognitive-mediators-of-metaphysical-commitment\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-r-b-s-unowned-recollections-provide-an-existence-proof-for-apparent-memory-conte--6a14bce7e1a3\\\",\n        \\\"claim-quasi-memory-accounts-must-specify-which-form-of-self-representation-is-required--4b048f888bc8\\\",\n        \\\"claim-episodic-recollection-can-preserve-temporally-and-spatially-situated-autobiograp--43867278649d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-does-not-entail-being-more-fundamental-than-so-appeals-to-relative-fun--0468a01c8a45\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Relations Without Simple Priority\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"R.B.'s unowned recollections create a natural bridge to debates about whether metaphysical relations must have strict-order structure. The memory source pressures simple views that episodic memory automatically grounds or guarantees personal identity, because apparent memory content can remain without felt ownership.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Grounding Beyond Strict Order\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The grounding-order source similarly challenges structural assumptions about grounding by arguing that grounding is not transitive, irreflexive, or asymmetric. Its truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding examples are used to show that intuitive direction or priority does not by itself settle the formal profile of grounding.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Comparative Use\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The cross-source synthesis is limited but useful: both sources warn against building metaphysical theory around an over-simple relational template. A page can compare identity-through-memory and ground-grounded relations as cases where intuitive direction, priority, or evidential force needs finer analysis.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Memory, Identity, and Relational Grounding\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-memory-identity-and-relational-grounding\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-trait-self-knowledge-can-remain-accurate-and-resilient-even-when-episodic-memory--e1d296edc23e\\\",\n        \\\"claim-r-b-retained-factual-self-knowledge-trait-self-knowledge-voluntary-scene-recall--fc36edde2153\\\",\n        \\\"claim-objectual-essence-can-be-accounted-for-through-generic-essence-so-a-feature-is-w--bd5daa95f779\\\",\n        \\\"claim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\\\",\n        \\\"claim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f\\\",\n        \\\"claim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\\\",\n        \\\"claim-ground-theoretic-status-is-preserved-under-factual-identity-because-the-proposed--4aecebbdb4a2\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Self-Knowledge Without Ownership\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The memory source supplies a focused topic on the distinction between episodic ownership and other forms of self-knowledge. Trait self-knowledge, factual self-knowledge, voluntary scene recall, and some future planning can remain in place even when past scenes no longer feel personally owned.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decomposing Identity Vocabulary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"This can be synthesized with the generalized-identity source because both distinguish different roles that may be conflated under one broad identity vocabulary. The metaphysical source separates generic essence, objectual essence, factual identity, and ground-theoretic status; the memory source separates event content, mineness, trait knowledge, and diachronic identity feeling.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Structural Overlap Only\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The conceptual overlap is structural rather than doctrinal. The page should not claim that generalized identity analyzes personal memory directly, but it can use the formal source as a contrast case for why identity claims often need decomposition into finer relations.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Self-Knowledge Without Episodic Ownership\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-self-knowledge-without-episodic-ownership\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
